nd it\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Requests are counted against the credential rather than the connection over a fixed window of 60 seconds.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Requests are counted against the credential rather than the connection over a fixed window of 60 seconds\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Opening additional sockets provides no benefit.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Opening additional sockets provides no benefit\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A client spread across worker processes is throttled at exactly the point a single process would be.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"a client spread across worker processes is throttled at exactly the point a single process would be\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 429 refusal is not an outage but the platform declining to spend capacity already promised to someone else.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"A 429 refusal is not an outage but the platform declining to spend capacity already promised to someone else\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Attempting to implement a client-side counter that mirrors the gateway's own creates two disagreeing counters.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Attempting to implement a client-side counter that mirrors the gateway's own creates two disagreeing counters\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Callers that retry immediately are the primary reason the cap exists.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Callers that retry immediately are the primary reason the cap exists\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Retry-After header value is a whole number of seconds.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Its value is a whole number of seconds\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Waiting the time specified in the Retry-After header and then continuing is the entire contract.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Waiting that long and then continuing is the entire contract\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A client that waits the time specified in the Retry-After header and then continues needs nothing else.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"a client that does it needs nothing else\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Waiting longer than the time specified in the Retry-After header earns no credit.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"waiting longer than the header asks earns no credit\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON and names the window, cap, and tier.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON and names the window, cap, and tier\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The body exists so a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"The body exists so a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic with information the caller does not have.\",\n      \"line\": 15,\n      \"span\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic with information the caller does not have\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The gateway does the same arithmetic on the 503 path.\",\n      \"line\": 15,\n      \"span\": \"it does the same on the 503 path\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A wait derived client-side is a guess about a counter the caller cannot see.\",\n      \"line\": 15,\n      \"span\": \"A wait derived client-side is a guess about a counter it cannot see\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 200 response needs nothing.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"A 200 needs nothing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 429 response needs the stated wait.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"a 429 needs the stated wait\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 500 response can be retried once that wait has passed.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"a 500 can be retried once that wait has passed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 503 response means the platform itself is overloaded.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"a 503 means the platform itself is overloaded\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"These response codes are not interchangeable.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"These cases are not interchangeable\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A client that folds all non-success responses into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"A client that folds all non-success responses into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"1000 is 50 times the default.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"which is 50 times the default\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The batch allowance is measured over exactly the same window, not a separate counting scheme.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"and is measured over exactly the same window, not a separate counting scheme\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A client written for one tier needs no change at all to run against the other.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"A client written for one tier needs no change at all to run against the other\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused cannot argue for a larger cap.\",\n      \"line\": 21,\n      \"span\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused cannot argue for a larger cap\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Nobody at the platform team will assemble that argument on behalf of a caller.\",\n      \"line\": 21,\n      \"span\": \"nobody at the platform team will assemble that argument on its behalf\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Not all refusals are caps.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"Not all refusals are caps\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three separate reasons.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three separate reasons\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Only one of those three reasons is a cap.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"only one of them is a cap\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A credential may be suspended.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"A credential may be suspended\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A route may be closed for maintenance.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"a route may be closed for maintenance\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A request body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Reading the status code rather than the error class is what separates these cases.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"Reading the status code rather than the error class is what separates these cases\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Reading the status code costs one comparison.\",\n      \"line\": 25,\n      \"span\": \"and it costs one comparison\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A cap can be raised, but not without measurement behind the request.\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"span\": \"A cap can be raised, but not without measurement behind the request\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty.\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"span\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A burst is cheaper to smooth than to serve at its peak.\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"span\": \"a burst is cheaper to smooth than to serve at its peak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all.\",\n 